// ReadOnly, and its absence cost a compile cycle on PipMonTestFacility.psc.
//
// `auto readonly` on a property is core FO4 Papyrus, not an extension, but the
// compiler still needs it DECLARED in this file or it rejects the property with
// "Unknown user flag readonly". Same rule as every other flag here, and it is
// not discoverable: nothing in the compiler output points at the flags file,
// and the properties that fail are ordinary-looking lines in the middle of a
// file. Worse, the failure is not local. The parser then mis-attributes every
// declaration after it, producing a dozen unrelated-looking errors -- a string
// literal "not viable", a duplicate variable, an '=' expecting a parenthesis --
// none of which have anything to do with the flag. Fixing the one flag cleared
// all of them.
//
// Note the comment syntax, because getting it wrong is the same mistake twice:
// this grammar accepts `//` only. A `;` comment is not a comment here, it is a
// parse error, and it takes PipMon.psc down with it even though PipMon.psc
// never mentions ReadOnly.
Flag ReadOnly 13
{
Property
}
